<title>FRANCE: TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN DOUBLES RESULTS.</title>
<headline>TENNIS-FRENCH OPEN DOUBLES RESULTS.</headline>
<dateline>PARIS 1997-05-29</dateline>
<text>
<p>Doubles results on the fourth day</p>
<p>of the French Open tennis tournament on Thursday.</p>
<p>Prefix number denotes seeding.</p>
<p>Men's doubles first round :</p>
<p>Joshua Eagle/Andrew Florent (Australia) beat Arnaud</p>
<p>Clement/Nicolas Escude (France) 4-6 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>Sander Groen/Jan Siemerink (Netherlands) beat 14-Donald</p>
<p>Johnson/Francisco Montana (U.S.) 2-6 7-6 (8-6) 6-4</p>
<p>Olivier Delaitre/Fabrice Santoro (France) beat Pablo Albano</p>
<p>(Argentina)/Peter Nyborg (Sweden) 3-6 7-6 (7-4) 6-4</p>
<p>Lucas Arnold/Daniel Orsanic (Argentina) beat Nebojsa Djordjevic</p>
<p>(Yugoslavia)/Doug Flach (U.S.) 6-2 6-1</p>
<p>6-Ellis Ferreira (South Africa)/Patrick Galbraith (U.S.) beat</p>
<p>Aleksandar Kitinov (Macedonia)/Greg Van Emburgh (U.S.) 6-3 6-2</p>
<p>10-Mark Philippoussis/Patrick Rafter (Australia) beat Brian</p>
<p>MacPhie (U.S.)/Gary Muller (South Africa) 6-7 (5-7) 7-6 (7-5)</p>
<p>8-6</p>
<p>Wayne Black (Zimbabwe)/Jim Grabb (U.S.) beat Kent Kinnear</p>
<p>(U.S.)/Pavel Vizner (Czech Republic) 6-3 7-6 (7-3)</p>
<p>Mahesh Bhupathi/Leander Paes (India) beat Dave Randall/Jack</p>
<p>Waite (U.S.) 6-2 6-2</p>
<p>Tom Kempers/Menno Oosting (Netherlands) beat Nuno Marques</p>
<p>(Portugal)/Tom Vanhoudt (Belgium) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>5-Sebastien Lareau (Canada)/Alex O'Brien (U.S.) beat Mark</p>
<p>Petchey (Britain)/David Rikl (Czech Republic) 6-4 7-6 (13-11)</p>
<p>Pat Cash (Australia)/Richey Reneberg (U.S.) beat Paul</p>
<p>Kilderry/Michael Tebbutt (Australia) 5-7 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Gustavo Kuerten/Fernando Meligeni (Brazil) beat Nicolas Pereira</p>
<p>(Venezuela)/Jeff Tarango (U.S.) 6-1 4-6 8-6</p>
<p>Karsten Braasch/Jens Knippschild (Germany) beat Hendrik Jan</p>
<p>Davids/Sjeng Schalken (Netherlands) 5-7 6-4 9-7</p>
<p>9-Jonas Bjorkman/Nicklas Kulti (Sweden) beat Sebastien</p>
<p>Grosjean/Olivier Mutis (France) 6-1 6-4</p>
<p>7-Rick Leach/Jonathan Stark (U.S.) beat Guillaume Marx/Olivier</p>
<p>Morel (France) 7-5 6-3</p>
<p>Women's doubles first round :</p>
<p>16-Ruxandra Dragomir (Romania)/Iva Majoli (Croatia) beat</p>
<p>Barbara Rittner (Germany)/Dominique Van Roost (Belgium) 6-4 6-2</p>
<p>11-Naoko Kijimuta/Nana Miyagi (Japan) beat Radka Bobkova/Eva</p>
<p>Melicharova (Czech Republic) 6-3 6-1</p>
<p>Emilie Loit/Amelie Mauresmo (France) beat Mariaan De Swardt</p>
<p>(South Africa)/Andrea Temesvari (Hungary) 6-3 6-4</p>
<p>6-Nicole Arendt (U.S.)/Manon Bollegraf (Netherlands) beat</p>
<p>Kirstin Freye (Germany)/Seda Noorlander (Netherlands) 6-1 6-0</p>
